9.1 Delayed Associative Recall Under Interference

Memory items  m_1, \ldots, m_N  are written into the system. The system is then subjected to delay  \Delta  and interference. A cue is subsequently presented:

\text{cue}_i \to \text{READ} \to \hat{m}_i

Performance is:

P(\hat{m}_i = m_i)

as a function of number of memories  N , delay  \Delta , interference, noise  \sigma , and observation bandwidth.

