Appendix E — Experimental Protocols

E.1 Phase Ic: Idle Decay Protocol

1. Write: Apply input sequence  u_{1:T}  encoding memory  m .
2. Quench: Stop all forcing (flow = 0, light = off). Record time  t_0 .
3. Wait: For delays  \Delta \in \{1 \text{ min}, 5 \text{ min}, 15 \text{ min}, 30 \text{ min}, 1 \text{ hr}, 2 \text{ hr}, 4 \text{ hr}\} , record observation  y_{t_0 + \Delta} .
4. Read: Apply decoder  D_\psi  to  y_{t_0 + \Delta}  to obtain  \hat{m} .
5. Estimate: Compute  I(m; \hat{m})  using the empirical distribution over many trials.
6. Fit: Compare decay models (exponential, power-law, step, oscillatory).

Controls: Measure system drift with no memory written (baseline noise). Measure sensor noise with a known state.

E.2 Phase Ia: WRITE Protocol Learning

1. Initialize: Random encoder  E_\phi  (neural network).
2. Simulate: Apply  u = E_\phi(m)  to the RNCRN simulator.
3. Observe: Record  y  after delay  \Delta .
4. Decode: Apply decoder  D_\psi  to obtain  \hat{m} .
5. Update: Gradient descent on  \|m - \hat{m}\|^2  with respect to  \phi  and  \psi .
6. Evaluate: Compare to random encoding baseline.

E.3 Phase Ib: READ Protocol Learning (Black-Box)

1. Freeze: The RNCRN dynamics  F  are hidden; only  y  is observable.
2. Explore: Agent selects inputs  u_t  from admissible set.
3. Observe: Receives  y_t = H(x_t) + \eta_t .
4. Reward:  R = -\|\hat{m} - m\|^2 .
5. Learn: Model-free RL (PPO, SAC) or evolution strategies.
6. Evaluate: Compare to oracle decoder with access to  F .

